# CDK's context cache. The usual advice is to COMMIT this so synth is
# reproducible, and for FIP the opposite is right: no stack may require a
# context lookup. FipMemberStack and FipAnalysisStack are deliberately
# account-agnostic so they synthesize with no credentials in the target
# account — a member account or a third-party examiner's tenant. A tracked
# context file would start empty, silently fill with account-specific
# lookups the first time someone synthesized with credentials, and then be
# committed as though it were part of the design.
cdk.context.json
